# Netlify publishes the repo root ("publish = ." in netlify.toml), which means
# every file in the project is reachable over HTTP — including the database
# schema and migrations. RLS is enforced server-side so this grants nobody
# access, but there is no reason to hand out the table shapes and security
# policies to anyone who guesses the path. robots.txt only asks crawlers not
# to look; this actually refuses.
/supabase/*    /index.html   404
